DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ppkkgg__ssuubbsstt is used within the ports tree to substitute variable values,
     using the exact same conventions used by pkg_create(1).  Constructs like
     ${VAR} will be replaced with the variable value, according to --DD
     _n_a_m_e[=_v_a_l_u_e] options.

     The options are as follows

     --BB _b_a_s_e_d_i_r        Specify a basedir in which we know file properties.  It
                       is forbidden to copy files from elsewhere without --mm
                       _m_o_d_e.

     --cc                Copy and substitute.  Number of _f_i_l_e arguments must be
                       even.  They are paired as _s_r_c_1 _d_e_s_t_1, _s_r_c_2 _d_e_s_t_2 _._._.
                       and each _s_r_c file is substituted and copied into the
                       corresponding _d_e_s_t file.

     --DD _n_a_m_e[=_v_a_l_u_e]   Define _n_a_m_e to _v_a_l_u_e, or to 1 if no value is given.

     --gg _g_r_o_u_p          Change group of destination file to _g_r_o_u_p.

     --ii                Ignore changes to group or owner that failed.

     --mm _m_o_d_e           Change mode of destination file to _m_o_d_e.

     --oo _o_w_n_e_r          Change owner of destination file to _o_w_n_e_r.

     If no _f_i_l_e arguments is given, ppkkgg__ssuubbsstt acts as a filter from stdin to
     stdout.

     Without --cc, each _f_i_l_e is backed up as _f_i_l_e_._b_e_f_o_r_e_s_u_b_s_t before the substi‐
     tution occurs.

